  "question": {
    "text": "Consider&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;non-zero vectors&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>c</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;such that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>⋅</mo><mover><mi>c</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. If a vector&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;satisfies the relation&nbsp;<math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>×</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>×</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover></math> and <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>⋅</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, then <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>⋅</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>×</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>⋅</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>×</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to"
  },
